# Approach 1 :

- Time complexity: $$O(NlogN)$$

- Space complexity: $$O(1)$$

# Code
```Java []
class Solution {
    public boolean stoneGame(int[] piles) {
        int n = piles.length;
        Arrays.sort(piles);
        int aliceScore = 0;
        int bobScore = 0;

        for (int i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            if (i % 2 == 1) {
                aliceScore += piles[i];
            } else {
                bobScore += piles[i];
            }
        }

        return (aliceScore > bobScore) ? true : false;
    }
}
```

